Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["From a Sullivan Model to an IBL Algebra", "Title",
 CellID->509267359,ExpressionUUID->"4ddb5767-1f00-4973-a411-49eacd07850d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The dIBL algebra of a closed oriented ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9f897693-7f3d-4f6a-bf8c-e302065939c6"],
 "-manifold ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "91d67f94-08f2-4756-84f3-94eee6576ea3"],
 " lives on the cyclic words of a graded alphabet, and the alphabet is a \
basis of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "*"], "(", 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "350fe529-9132-41c4-807d-3105f4aa2fe8"],
 " shifted by one, with the pairing that Poincar\[EAcute] duality gives it. \
This tutorial builds that alphabet without ever mentioning ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77f49707-c9fd-4b58-a29f-c6a521aa721d"],
 ": it starts from a Sullivan minimal model, puts the natural orientation on \
it, checks that the resulting oriented PDGA is of Hodge type, passes to the \
nondegenerate quotient, and reads the canonical Maurer-Cartan element off the \
triple product of the quotient. The running example is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["CP",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f359076b-8842-42ab-8005-e8d8ccdd169a"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9d47005c-b7e4-4454-ae7b-908d64881c13"],

Cell["Five steps, and each one is a single function.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f3053b8c-1021-4564-87d0-ccb771bd1e43"],

Cell["The minimal model", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"fda1ec98-6bd7-4f30-b892-a833d9b57ffd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A Sullivan minimal model is a free graded commutative algebra ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalLambda]", 
    StyleBox["U", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c604e2e6-8dfa-4fea-a292-3a2e1f8e6d31"],
 " with a differential. For ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["CP",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2219955c-af27-4972-a519-d00cf216aa86"],
 " it has two generators: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ae65061f-79fb-4c98-896e-46c8d0e07a2f"],
 " in degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["2", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dbd360c8-db71-4132-8ae9-d1520ab3f889"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cc1a763f-6c9c-4bf3-89ee-413fd6b114f6"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29ca5932-bc0e-452c-a63f-ae7c02cbc471"],
 " in degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], "+", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "497c23ac-deee-4289-944c-5c12a50b24f6"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["m", "TI"], "+", "1"}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76b5b8f3-66ed-4db4-84cb-aec7042cf33b"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d8c3801e-99a0-4aa8-bfc2-05646e366eaf"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"model", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"SullivanModel", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<ComplexProjectiveSpace\>\"", "[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
  RowBox[{"model", "[", "\"\<Generators\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"06d36ab9-54f9-4c71-828e-5703af0e9db7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"a", "\[Rule]", "2"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"b", "\[Rule]", "5"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[1]= ",ExpressionUUID->"cc2fb087-479d-4890-8de6-04e6d39dbdb7"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The differential is stored on the generators and extended as a derivation. It \
raises degree by one:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"692a568d-dd83-4b10-84fd-b6aff38ce92c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"SullivanModelDifferential", "[", 
    RowBox[{"b", ",", " ", "model"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"SullivanModelDifferential", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"a", " ", "b"}], ",", " ", "model"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"45affeb4-199a-49e8-9b6c-a3b6a74c50e4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["a", "3"], ",", 
   SuperscriptBox["a", "4"]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[2]= ",ExpressionUUID->"a7cc7760-5145-46bb-9bfc-baca70c4804d"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A monomial is written as a product of generators, read in the order the \
model declares them. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["SullivanModelBasis"]], 
    "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/SullivanModelBasis", "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "def895ee-be46-42ec-845f-6748bfe7c157"],
 " lists the monomials of one degree; the algebra is infinite-dimensional, \
one or two monomials in every degree from here up."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0ca4cea9-03c3-40af-9aa5-d898ff070c68"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"SullivanModelBasis", "[", 
    RowBox[{"model", ",", " ", "k"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "8"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"da402e86-0183-44f7-9168-7078f1312bbe"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", "a", "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    SuperscriptBox["a", "2"], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", "b", "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    SuperscriptBox["a", "3"], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"a", " ", "b"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    SuperscriptBox["a", "4"], "}"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[3]= ",ExpressionUUID->"e5a806b9-6d35-4824-a258-90ce7d3c0e4f"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["The orientation, and the pairing it defines", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5c85f806-a07b-42ae-994f-92e47b7eb2ac"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The cohomology of this model is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["R",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "]"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "3"], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c3f1ee7a-de65-493f-94a3-5025f07c04d9"],
 ", so the top class is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "26842f80-fae8-4559-bb2a-2c7f617994e9"],
 " in degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "45950cbb-92c3-4223-be72-5dba7a6ed474"],
 ". Let the orientation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ed88769-b465-4a9a-946e-5da2a1050864"],
 " be the coefficient of that monomial: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["1", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9a26bb5c-c8d0-4621-a147-0ae5650fa8aa"],
 " on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c8095eef-7e69-4db8-a41a-6e7bbb66d939"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["0", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fbf39323-d540-40ac-8454-03513c3547dd"],
 " on everything else. That is what ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"model", "[", "\"\<Orientation\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "73270fc2-4d30-4e4a-8f11-adc53d8b2a5b"],
 " records, as its values on the monomials of degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ec527af4-645d-47eb-a6bc-2ab2c66426bb"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9b04c9e8-063b-48f7-bf34-e1c1f8d6bd1e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"model", "[", "\"\<Orientation\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"model", "[", "\"\<Degree\>\"", "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"71ccf89a-2859-4606-9f99-76802ecb82e1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["a", "2"], "\[Rule]", "1"}], "\[RightAssociation]"}], ",",
    "4"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[4]= ",ExpressionUUID->"f1e386da-9877-40e9-9d92-f5877d61d643"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["SullivanModelOrientation"]], 
    "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/SullivanModelOrientation", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9228e4a2-0f0e-4822-86eb-64cf48d8a288"],
 " applies it. Everything outside degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c6166519-7b42-4f86-9d1c-b8e128c9d128"],
 " is killed, and inside degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "32f7c888-b792-4249-9860-6d903e62fbd4"],
 " only ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1cbccbba-ce1f-4972-8b48-57f8dc0256ca"],
 " survives:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cc9d972a-014f-4f8c-bba9-e3b670070235"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"SullivanModelOrientation", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"a", "^", "2"}], ",", " ", "model"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"SullivanModelOrientation", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"a", "^", "3"}], ",", " ", "model"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"SullivanModelOrientation", "[", 
    RowBox[{"b", ",", " ", "model"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"f0c2abd4-8fe7-4aea-ad8a-066e779e52d0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"1", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[5]= ",ExpressionUUID->"41958a2c-f827-4d8d-a17c-4993b9448d88"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The pairing is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[LeftAngleBracket]", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["v", "TI"], "1"], ",", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["v", "TI"], "2"]}], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
    
    StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["v", "TI"], "1"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["v", "TI"], "2"]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58887037-ba1a-4d76-81b0-2713d8b90c58"],
 ", the orientation of the product. On ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"1", ",", 
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], ",", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "2"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b41aa49a-1aea-441a-830d-8a0f1619bc44"],
 " it is the antidiagonal, which is Poincar\[EAcute] duality:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"63a5a0c6-afe1-4cfc-a72c-587a2649801b"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"SullivanModelPairing", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"a", "^", "i"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"a", "^", "j"}], ",", " ", "model"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"i", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "//", 
  " ", "MatrixForm"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7705598d-a533-4ba8-b94b-bd46fbd4eb21"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", GridBox[{
     {"0", "0", "1"},
     {"0", "1", "0"},
     {"1", "0", "0"}
    },
    GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Center}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {
        Offset[0.27999999999999997`], {
         Offset[0.7]}, 
        Offset[0.27999999999999997`]}, "Rows" -> {
        Offset[0.2], {
         Offset[0.4]}, 
        Offset[0.2]}}], "\[NoBreak]", ")"}],
  Function[BoxForm`e$, 
   MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[6]= ",ExpressionUUID->"d7ff3722-28a0-4746-9639-c002004e9607"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is an ",
 StyleBox["orientation", "TI"],
 " in the sense of Lambrechts-Stanley: it has degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ac4eb3c3-c326-4569-9646-8df8ba4c382a"],
 ", it kills the image of the differential, and it does not vanish on the \
kernel. Together with the perfect pairing it induces on cohomology, that \
makes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalLambda]", 
     StyleBox["U", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["d",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], ",", 
     StyleBox["O", "TI"]}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9d947d17-7138-49c9-baa5-e170a3450d88"],
 " an oriented PDGA of degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d2d82de4-3c1c-42d3-adb9-60cbc958d49a"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"77d756da-07a8-41e6-95f2-c18b4c9d7763"],

Cell["Is it of Hodge type?", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3b200831-e6c4-4556-ad2c-2331d32e3e16"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The pairing is ",
 StyleBox["not", "TI"],
 " perfect on chain level: the whole of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalLambda]", 
    StyleBox["U", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f8cd6e11-bbfc-4820-99d7-e72a329c9aa3"],
 " above degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30af28ea-e74a-4332-937e-4074efd98948"],
 " is paired to zero with everything, because the orientation only sees \
degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cb29c3d3-8321-4ec7-9d44-d144b3b8e097"],
 ". Those elements form the ",
 StyleBox["degenerate subspace", "TI"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["deg",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d02f9760-f650-43ec-b781-ef55f94afe8d"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8a9dae66-c102-4d3d-8439-da3cc4ca1ce3"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"DegenerateSubspace", "[", 
    RowBox[{"model", ",", " ", "5"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"DegenerateSubspace", "[", 
    RowBox[{"model", ",", " ", "6"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"DegenerateSubspace", "[", 
    RowBox[{"model", ",", " ", "7"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"df739d8b-d24c-4c9e-b830-b5cc6bb42be1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "b", "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    SuperscriptBox["a", "3"], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"a", " ", "b"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[7]= ",ExpressionUUID->"3bad02b0-24a4-4a8f-a7d0-542bd722fd55"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The oriented PDGA is ",
 StyleBox["of Hodge type", "TI"],
 " when it admits a Hodge decomposition ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], "\[CirclePlus]", 
    StyleBox["im",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
    StyleBox["d",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[CirclePlus]", 
    StyleBox["C", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0049e42f-7784-4d6d-a808-0b4ee0e1a652"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["C", "TI"], "\[Perpendicular]", 
    StyleBox["C", "TI"], "\[CirclePlus]", 
    StyleBox["H", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "82128cd6-ec42-408a-9fba-327a989629a9"],
 ". Over a field of characteristic ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[NotEqual]", "2"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "92544553-d5ed-48e9-a313-2b12f9f751e5"],
 " and for a quotient of finite type, that happens exactly when ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["deg",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5a58b82c-9b05-4fc7-8bc7-8ab1395f7f44"],
 " is acyclic, equivalently exactly when the quotient map onto the \
nondegenerate quotient is a quasi-isomorphism. So the test is one cohomology \
computation."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7b0d4f3d-6bab-4665-a730-c9f6b121ba33"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"HodgeTypeQ", "[", "model", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"222988d6-780e-4cd8-bde0-7c09f28247d1"],

Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[8]= ",ExpressionUUID->"04cbe296-3f4d-4577-a89a-a661b13cf412"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["HodgeTypeReport"]], "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/HodgeTypeReport", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "24a3b698-5433-4998-87b8-246e6b605cb4"],
 " shows why, degree by degree. The fourth column is the cohomology of the \
degenerate subspace, and it vanishes throughout. Here the second and fifth \
columns agree as well, which says more: the quotient carries no differential, \
so it ",
 StyleBox["is", "TI"],
 " the cohomology: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["CP",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4af9175e-5553-4fc6-aff5-e3bb2cd9d037"],
 " is formal. A Hodge-type model whose quotient keeps a differential has ",
 Cell[BoxData["Cohomology"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "097ca59e-b45e-484d-b387-0d0c01c02b64"],
 " strictly below ",
 Cell[BoxData["Quotient"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1de32992-fbd3-41fd-b84b-831a77c26140"],
 ", and the next tutorial shows one."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d7d061a1-1c4d-4a24-b06c-c9eeca8e6f4e"],

